          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly avows Pierre's present loving state toward Hélène. Its conventional and embarrassed delivery may bear on sincerity or depth, but does not remove its clear truth-conditional avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":1,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.82,\"reason\":\"The words contain no explicit promise or stated terms. In this betrothal setting, however, Pierre weakly enacts or ratifies his socially expected role as Hélène's fiancé by supplying the expected declaration. Any undertaking is Pierre's implicit acceptance of that relationship, not an independent promise created clearly by the sentence. Hélène gives no subsequent verbal uptake in the supplied scene, although the couple have already been treated as engaged and later marry.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The expression is not represented as a reflexive affective outburst. Pierre deliberately recalls and produces what he believes convention requires, and the narration emphasizes its inadequate sound rather than spontaneous discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"No distinct core function remains beyond the direct avowal and the weak contextual ratification of the betrothal. Embarrassment, convention, and social pressure qualify the delivery but are not separate force modes.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Hélène and Pierre have publicly been treated and congratulated as an engaged couple, they are left alone. Hélène kisses Pierre, and he then addresses her with the expected French declaration of love, consciously recalling what one is supposed to say in such circumstances.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The target explicitly avows love but does not state a promise. At most, Pierre weakly ratifies his expected position as Hélène's fiancé. No direct response by Hélène after this utterance is supplied; her kiss precedes it. Their marriage a month and a half later confirms the broader betrothal's outcome but does not turn the focal sentence itself into a clear marriage promise.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"I recognize the supplied passage as an excerpt from Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace. The classification relies only on the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly establishes the avowal's linguistic force and shows attraction alongside hesitation and social pressure. It does not conclusively settle the depth, durability, or sincerity of Pierre's love, nor whether Hélène specifically understood this sentence as creating an obligation.\"}"
